    "body": "progress: bherbruck · 2026-11-07T23:25:57Z · committed on issue/187-wcs-321 (fork): `pick::align_321` + an \"Align WCS (3-2-1)\" button under the Geometry picks (flat face → Z outward, straight edge → X in that plane, vertex or bore centre → origin on the face; else the edge's start), placed through the existing undoable `SetWcs`. Pinned by `wcs_align` (5 tests: square block, far-end origin flips X, a block turned 30° aligns to its own edge and the angles round-trip, a side face tilts Z, every missing/doubled datum refused by name) and the UI test `face_origin::align_wcs_321_places_g54_from_the_face_and_edge_picks` - all pass. Gate running; PR follows (a feat, merges at the next cut). Note: its shell snapshot changes overlap PR #188's, so whichever merges second regenerates them.",
